Replaces the 29-line 3-layer scaffold stub with the full Model 6
implementation that was previously staged (but never applied) inside
wt-pm-dbn-feature-extraction:

- model.py: 6-layer bias-free encoder (Linear 64→128→96→64→48→32→rep_dim,
  LeakyReLU 0.1, Kaiming init), init_center, svdd_loss, anomaly_score,
  train_svdd, plus a 24-turbine synthetic farm (16 physical channels,
  6 incipient fault types, chronological split), ZCA whitening, fixed
  20-epoch Adam training, 99th-percentile threshold with 3-hour
  persistence alarm rule, per-fault delay reporting, and comparisons
  against the original scaffold and Mahalanobis baseline.
- requirements.txt: reduced to torch, numpy (scikit-learn was unused).
- results/model6_metrics.json: seed-42 metrics (AUROC 0.865, F1 0.718,
  12/12 events detected, median delay 65.5 h).
- results/model6_seed_sweep.json: six-seed sweep showing Model 6 leads
  the scaffold and Mahalanobis on AUROC (0.885±0.016), F1 (0.782±0.038),
  events detected (68/72) and median delay (56.5 h).
- README.md: full model description, structure, setup, results table,
  platform contract, honest limits.
- index.html, docs/index.html: updated landing page with m13-deep-svdd
  adapter card and working View-on-GitHub link.

API surface for the wt-pm platform adapter is preserved:
DeepSVDDNetwork(input_dim, rep_dim), init_center(model, [(X,)]),
svdd_loss(model(X), model.c).
